{
 "id": "pi-wall-mount-petg",
 "batch": 3,
 "brief": "A wall mount for a Raspberry Pi 4 in PETG (FDM, printed flat, layers along Z). The wall is the plane z = 0; two M4 screws go into it at x = -49 and x = +49 (y = 0) through a 5 mm plate. The board's four M2.5 holes (58 x 49 mm pattern, centred on the origin) sit on 6 mm round standoffs whose tops are at z = 9, with M2.5 screws threaded into 2.2 mm pilot holes in them. The board's underside needs 2 mm clear under it (85 x 56 mm, centred). The mount stays inside x = -55 to 55, y = -35 to 35, z = 0 to 9. Plugging a cable in pushes 40 N on the board toward the wall; pulling one out pulls 30 N away from the wall; yanking one sideways pulls 25 N along X at 6 mm above the standoff tops. Safety factor 2.",
